## Context
Rule `rules/coding-python.md` (branch python-env-rules, commits b626fd56 and 7d4fd719) states one uv-based environment practice: dependencies in pyproject.toml with a committed uv.lock, no pip, one `RUN` prefix in the Makefile and no PYTHON variable. On 2026-10-23 the alignment check below ran on ten Python repos (the nine in ~/CNRS/code and sen-causal-reading): five print ok, five do not: sen-causal-reading (its own ticket 0083 and PR, in its own repo) and the four children below. Impact is real only for sen-causal-reading, where `project-state.py --tests` reports a false failure; the four children are deviations, not breakages, ticketed at the author's request (2026-10-23) although they sit under the severity floor.

## Children
- 1207 askMinh
- 1208 VN-Power-Scenario (third-party remote: author's decision needed before any push)
- 1209 ThinkTanksSurveyor (not a git repository)
- 1210 fs-housekeeper
- sen-causal-reading: ticket 0083 in that repo, not tracked here

## Alignment check
One line per repo, run from the repo root; prints `ok` when aligned. It took 0.2 s over all five repos on 2026-10-23.
```
[ -f uv.lock ] && ! grep -qE "^[[:space:]]*PYTHON[[:space:]]*[?:]?=" Makefile 2>/dev/null && ! grep -qs "pip install" Makefile README.md && { [ ! -f requirements.txt ] || head -1 requirements.txt | grep -q autogenerated; } && echo ok
```
A requirements.txt is accepted only when its first line says it is autogenerated by uv; whether sen-causal-reading keeps such a generated file is the open decision of its PR.

## Verification cadence
No new probe in project-state.py (author, 2026-10-23). Because the check is that fast, it belongs to /lair if it is run periodically; whether /lair gains a step for it is open. Until then this tracker, open while any child is open, is the reminder.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Children 1207-1210 closed or consciously dropped, each with the alignment check printing `ok` or a stated reason it does not apply
- [ ] sen-causal-reading ticket 0083 merged or dropped by its author
- [ ] Integration: the check prints `ok` in every repo not dropped
